### Step 5

Join every tuple.

| Tuple     | After `join()` |
| --------- | -------------- |
| ('a','d') | "ad"           |
| ('a','e') | "ae"           |
| ('a','f') | "af"           |
| ('b','d') | "bd"           |
| ('b','e') | "be"           |
| ('b','f') | "bf"           |
| ('c','d') | "cd"           |
| ('c','e') | "ce"           |
| ('c','f') | "cf"           |

Final answer

```python
[
"ad",
"ae",
"af",
"bd",
"be",
"bf",
"cd",
"ce",
"cf"
]
```